# Allowlist for scripts/ci/no-private-refs.sh — a security decision, not a convenience.
#
# One rule per line, `path/glob:pattern  # justification`. The glob matches the repo-relative
# path; the pattern is an ERE matched against the whole `git grep` hit (`path:line:text`).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. A justification is mandatory in review.
#
# ⛔ Do NOT add an entry to keep a real internal hostname, address or private repository path in
# a public tree. Remove it. An entry is only for a string that *looks* private but is not (e.g. a
# documented loopback example, or a term that collides with a pattern).
#
# No entries today on purpose: every current hit is real and is the cleanup session's to scrub
# (see #54). The guard is expected to fail until that scrub lands.
#
# The three rules below are NOT a scrub exemption — they cover the redaction machinery itself,
# which necessarily spells the patterns out (same reason this guard excludes its own script):
# a page generator has to name `*.internal` to redact it, and its checker has to assert it.
docs/design/scripts/build-docs.py:re\.compile          # the redaction rules, not a reference
docs/design/scripts/check-docs.cjs:\.internal hostname # the assertion label, not a reference
docs/design/studio.css:agent-avatar\.internal          # CSS class name, not a hostname
